Bundled third-party software
----------------------------

This package bundles its own copies of Qt 6 and other third-party libraries
under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib so that it runs independently of the Qt version
installed on the system.

Copyright and license texts for the bundled system libraries (harvested from
the distribution packages they were deployed from at build time) are shipped
under /opt/plotjuggler4/share/doc/<package>/.

Qt 6 is used under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3
(/usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-3); FFmpeg is built with an LGPL-only feature
set and used under the LGPL, version 2.1 or later
(/usr/share/common-licenses/LGPL-2.1). Their license texts are not duplicated
inside /opt. The remaining bundled libraries come from the project's pinned
Conan dependency set (assimp, draco, luau, cpython, and others) under their
respective permissive or LGPL licenses.

Corresponding sources for the LGPL components: the exact versions and build
configuration are pinned in the PlotJuggler 4 repository (versions.env,
conanfile.txt, conan.lock, recipes/), from which each component's unmodified
upstream source release can be retrieved; the sources are also available on
written request via https://github.com/PlotJuggler/PJ4/issues. The bundled Qt
and FFmpeg shared libraries under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib can be replaced with
user-built compatible versions, satisfying the LGPL relinking requirement.

Bundled plugins under /opt/plotjuggler4/lib/plotjuggler/plugins are published
separately by the PlotJuggler project and carry their own license metadata in
each plugin's manifest.json.

Retro render helper (/opt/plotjuggler4/bin/3rdparty/retro)
-----------------------------------------------------------

pj-raster-helper is an independent executable that PlotJuggler launches as a
child process and links no part of. It is licensed under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 (/usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-2), whose full text also
ships next to the binary as COPYING. Its complete corresponding source —
raster/helper/ in the PlotJuggler 4 repository plus the doomgeneric submodule
pinned there — is covered by the written offer in SOURCE-OFFER.txt, shipped in
the same directory.

base.wad is id Software's unmodified DOOM1.WAD shareware data, redistributed
under the terms in SHAREWARE-LICENSE.txt, shipped in the same directory. It is
data, not a program: no part of PlotJuggler or of the helper is derived from
it.
